It was deployed with Aravind Eye Hospital in India and has been used at huge scale. Google reported more than **200,000 patients screened**, while subsequent reporting of post-deployment performance at Aravind covered hundreds of thousands of screenings. ([blog.google][3])

ARDA was trained using retinal photographs from both the **US and India** and subsequently validated in other populations. ([PubMed Central (PMC)][4])

Recent Indian post-deployment data is particularly impressive:

* severe NPDR/PDR sensitivity: **97.0%**
* specificity: **96.4%**
* STDR sensitivity: **95.9%**
