# 20. One more feature that could REALLY impress judges

## **AI Uncertainty / "Don't Know" Mode**

This is a very mature AI feature.

Most student projects try to say:

> "Our AI is 98% accurate."

Instead, your AI should be allowed to say:

> ⚠️ **I am not confident enough to classify this image.**

For example:

```text
Prediction
Moderate DR

Confidence
61%

Image Quality
Poor

Recommendation
DO NOT TRUST AUTOMATED RESULT

→ Refer for human review
```

This is actually **more medically responsible**.

And it connects directly with the real-world problem that image quality can make AI outputs unreliable. Recent studies show image acquisition and ungradable images remain important barriers. ([Nature][10])

